            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="fb-stage-block"><span class="fb-stage-label">What you do</span><p>Reach the back teeth on both sides, where buildup tends to collect. Keep the same time of day so it becomes part of the evening.</p></div>
          <div class="fb-stage-block"><span class="fb-stage-label">What you learn</span><p>How to use the wipe itself as a check on what you're removing, and why yellowing that doesn't change may be tartar for your vet to look at.</p></div>
        </article>
        {%- comment -%} Stage 3 {%- endcomment -%}
        <article class="fb-stage-card">
          <div class="fb-stage-top">
            <div class="fb-stage-meta">
              <span class="fb-stage-kicker">Stage 3</span>
              <span class="fb-stage-range">Days 22–30</span>
              <span class="fb-stage-name">The new normal</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fb-heatmap" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- for d in (1..30) -%}<span style="background:{% if d < 22 %}#47B5E9{% elsif d <= 30 %}#13B6B5{% else %}#EAF6FD{% endif %};"></span>{%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="fb-stage-block"><span class="fb-stage-label">What you do</span><p>Treat it as maintenance rather than a project: the same short routine, most evenings, even on busy ones.</p></div>
          <div class="fb-stage-block"><span class="fb-stage-label">What you learn</span><p>Why consistency matters more than intensity, what to keep an eye on, and what to raise at your dog's next checkup.</p></div>
